{
  "_README": [
    "Fixture content for the documentation forge (v2.163.0). The product's own",
    "seeds are translated by the product (a board's column names, API Studio's",
    "starter collection); what lives here is the CONTENT a staged scene holds —",
    "the card titles on the board, the rows in the database grid, the labels on",
    "the infra canvas — so a translated guide shows that language's own context",
    "and not English data under translated chrome.",
    "",
    "Not shipped inside the IDE: these are documentation strings, and the",
    "product's translated surface should hold only what a user can actually see.",
    "scripts/docs-shots.sh passes this file to the forge as -Dnmox.shots.fixtures;",
    "a language with no entry falls back to 'en' SECTION BY SECTION, and",
    "ForgeFixturesGateTest fails the build when a shipped language is missing.",
    "",
    "THESE ARE NOT TRANSLATIONS. Each language's cards, names and cities are its",
    "own plausible work and its own people and places — that is the whole point.",
    "Two translators read one English card as 'shorten' and the rest as 'remove';",
    "both are a real card a developer would write, so both stay. Only the SHAPE",
    "is shared: the same sections, the same number of cards and rows.",
    "",
    "Fixed by design, and so exempt from the gate's copies-English check:",
    "  db.query   — SQL keywords and identifiers are code a developer retypes",
    "               (the v2.104.0 machine-text rule). Identical in every language.",
    "  infra.dns  — a hostname. Its first label MAY be the reader's own word for",
    "               a shop; the .example.com suffix never changes (RFC 2606).",
    "",
    "Two strings are one storyline and must stay so: the to-do card about naming",
    "the empty states is the card whose blocker asks design for that copy.",
    "",
    "The board's clock runs on the FIRST 'doing' card — the fixture names no card",
    "twice. An earlier draft carried a 'clocked' key repeating a card's title,",
    "which is one fact in two places kept byte-identical by hand across fifteen",
    "files; the defect is the second home, not the disagreement (v2.131.0).",
    "",
    "v2.164.0: inventory is the script the debugger picture pauses in, one",
    "item name per line so the breakpoint's line never moves; page is the shop",
    "front the DevTools picture picks from. The brand, Meridian, is a name and",
    "is not in the file."
  ],
